{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-359628-r4515936","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Banana Pecan Bread","sourcePageId":359628,"sourceRevision":"4515936","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T23:01:12Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Banana%20Pecan%20Bread&oldid=4515936","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:56.684Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for banana bread","Category:Recipes from Foodista","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using banana","Category:Recipes using butter","Category:Recipes using cooking spray","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using pecan","Category:Recipes using white sugar","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"fb4a74a0882fe2c966be836ad51585b4c20be068295a89862c95219f784a35cb","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Cake recipes\n| Servings = 8 servings\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n[http://www.foodista.com/recipe/GXJMCG8T/banana-pecan-bread Originally posted to Foodista] by Wendi Spraker. Foodista recipes are released under a [http://www.foodista.com/static/legal CC-BY license].\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Flour|all-purpose flour]], [[Cookbook:Sifter|sifted]]\n*3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*½ cup (1 stick) [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], room temperature\n*1 cup white [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]], room temperature and beaten\n*2 [[Cookbook:Banana|bananas]] (a little over-ripe is best)\n*1 tsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*1 cup chopped [[Cookbook:Pecan|pecans]]\n\n==Preparation==\n#Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to 325°F. Prepare [[Cookbook:Loaf Pan|loaf pan]] by using [[Cookbook:Cooking Spray|baking spray]]. Sift together the flour, baking powder and salt.\n#In the bowl of a stand [[Cookbook:Mixer|mixer]], [[Cookbook:Cream|cream]] together the butter, sugar and eggs on medium speed.\n#Add the bananas and lemon juice and mix until creamy.\n#Add the dry ingredients to the wet ingredients, then mix until just combined. \n#Turn the mixer off, scrape down the sides, reset to medium and mix for another minute.\n#Add the pecans and mix for about 20 seconds.\n#Turn into the prepared 1 ½ lb loaf pan. [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 60–75 minutes at 325°F.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using banana]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pecan]]\n[[Category:Recipes from Foodista]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for banana bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cooking spray]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]","isRecipe":false,"recipe":{"name":"Banana Pecan Bread","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"8 servings","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups all-purpose flour, sifted","sourceText":"2 cups all-purpose flour, sifted","amountText":"2 cups all-purpose flour, sifted","amount":null